{"blocks":[["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2098","buttons that move the highlighted scene up and down",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation","The strip has:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2155","a scene number box, best mapped to an endless encoder, for scrolling through scenes",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation","The strip has:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2244","a button that launches the highlighted scene; with Select Next Scene on Launch on in the Record, Warp & Launch Settings, each press moves on to the next scene",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation","The strip has:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2412","a button that cancels a triggered scene launch",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation","The strip has:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2464","one button per track that launches that track's clip in the highlighted scene",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation","The strip has:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2547","Live keeps the highlighted scene centered in Session View, which helps in large Sets.",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.1 Relative Session View Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2637","34.2.4.2 Mapping to Clip View Controls",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/04%20Mapping%20to%20Relative%20MIDI%20Controllers/","source-block-2787","Clip View shows whichever clip is selected, or several clips at once, so a mapping to a Clip View control can change any clip in the Set. The manual recommends relative controllers for Clip View controls to avoid jumps.",["34.2.4 Mapping to Relative MIDI Controllers","34.2.4.2 Mapping to Clip View Controls"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/05%20Computer%20Keyboard%20Remote%20Control/","source-block-290","34.2.5 Computer Keyboard Remote Control",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/05%20Computer%20Keyboard%20Remote%20Control/","source-block-560","1. Turn on Key Map Mode with the KEY switch in the upper right corner (Cmd+K on Mac, Ctrl+K on Windows). Mappable controls turn red and the Mapping Browser appears.",["34.2.5 Computer Keyboard Remote Control"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/34%20MIDI%20and%20Key%20Remote/02%20The%20Mapping%20Browser/05%20Computer%20Keyboard%20Remote%20Control/","source-block-736","2. Click the control to map; only controls with a red overlay can be mapped.",["34.2.5 Computer Keyboard Remote Control"]]],"format_version":5}